// GENERATED by gen_fused.py from idx2f_cand.cu (do not edit; edit the source or the generator). 4 rows per wgmma (N = 128), 3 math warpgroups.
// indexer2f: a copy of an earlier ds41h candidate-logits kernel (IDX_CAND v1, not in production's ds41h kernels);
// only the namespace / extension name changed (idx2f_cand).
// Used on owned sequences: each GPU scores only its own sequences' candidate union against its own compact index-K pages.

// IDX_CAND:
// candidate-only indexer scoring for the DeepSeek-V4.1 candidate-consumer layers (24/28/32/36).
//
// Stock (vLLM 0.32.0 sparse_attn_indexer.py:825-876, decode branch) on those layers:
//   logits = DeepGEMM sm90_fp8_paged_mqa_logits over the WHOLE row [0, row_end)   (dense, ~65K positions/row)
//   apply_candidate_mask(logits, row_end, layer-20 candidate blocks)               (-inf outside the <= 2,048 blocks of 8)
//   top-512 over [0, row_end)                                                      (persistent/sampled/cooperative)
// Here:
//   prep   : per request (NEXT_N consecutive rows) the ascending, de-duplicated union of the rows' candidate blocks that lie
//            inside the row ([0, ceil(row_end/8)) -- exactly the blocks the stock mask keeps), each row's ascending block
//            list (cblk) and compact length (clen = #positions the stock mask leaves finite in [0, row_end)).
//   logits : the SAME arithmetic as DeepGEMM's sm90_fp8_paged_mqa_logits<NEXT_N, 32, 128, 64, true, false, 3, 3, 256, 128,
//            512, M> (vllm/third_party/deep_gemm, JIT instantiations in DG_JIT_CACHE_DIR) but only on the union tiles:
//            64-token tiles = 8 candidate blocks gathered by 8 TMA boxes of [8 tokens x 128 B] into one 128B-swizzled
//            [64 x 128] fp8 tile (identical smem layout to the dense 64-token page tile), the identical WGMMA
//            (MMA_64x{32 * min(NEXT_N, 2)}x32 F32E4M3E4M3 SS, 4 k-steps, scale_d = k != 0) with the identical Q / weight
//            layout (rows paired exactly like the dense kernel's 2-CTA cluster split), and the dense epilogue copied verbatim
//            (relu * weight, 4-way intra-thread sums, * kv scale, 2 xor-shuffles). Values go to a compact row per query row:
//            compact[row, 8 * rank_row(block) + offset], i.e. the row's candidate positions in ascending position order.
//            Compiled with DeepGEMM's JIT flags (no --use_fast_math).
//   remap  : after the (stock) top-k over the compact rows: compact index t -> position 8 * cblk[row, t >> 3] + (t & 7).
// Why the selected set is the dense one: every position the dense top-k can see as finite is a compact
// entry with the bit-identical value, all other dense entries are -inf (never selected while >= k finite entries exist), and
// the compaction map is strictly increasing, so key order AND index order are preserved; rows with <= 2,048 blocks give a
// compact row identical to the dense row [0, row_end).
// CUDA-graph safe: no allocation, no host sync; every data-dependent bound is read on the device.
